# UBSan runtime suppressions for vendored code only; our own code gets none.
#   UBSAN_OPTIONS=suppressions=engines/sanitizers/ubsan.supp:halt_on_error=1
# Vendored files stay byte-identical (third_party/mutable/UPSTREAM.md), so
# each entry names upstream files and the reason the report is not a defect.
#
# Braids and stmlib's fixed-point DSP multiply and shift signed integers the
# way the modules' ARM GCC build did: products that wrap, and left shifts of
# negative values (`(x - 8192) << 1`). The Makefile compiles all vendored
# Mutable code with -fwrapv, which defines wrapping for the compiler; UBSan
# still reports it, because it checks the C++ rules rather than the build's.
signed-integer-overflow:third_party/mutable/braids/*
shift-base:third_party/mutable/braids/*
signed-integer-overflow:third_party/mutable/stmlib/utils/dsp.h
# Plaits' six-op Pow2Fast shifts by a negative exponent for very low levels;
# the result is discarded or tiny (engines/plaits-heavy.md, quirk 4).
shift-base:third_party/mutable/plaits/dsp/fm/dx_units.h
shift-exponent:third_party/mutable/plaits/dsp/fm/dx_units.h
# Peaks' bouncing ball shifts a negative initial velocity left by 4
# (set_initial_velocity), as ARM GCC compiled it; only fm1-mod-mi-ref runs
# the original, as the oracle for the Bounce kind's port, which multiplies
# by 16 instead (engines/mod/kinds.md).
shift-base:third_party/mutable/peaks/modulations/bouncing_ball.h
# msfa (FM6, engines/msfa.md) keeps its operator phases in int32_t and lets
# them wrap (fm_core.cc, fm_op_kernel.cc), and shifts negative values left
# (pitchenv.cc's `pitchtab[...] << 19`, dx7note.cc's ScaleVelocity), as its
# ARM and x86 builds did; built with -fwrapv. Felucca's fm6_core.c, the
# FM6 oracle (desktop test tool only), adds a modulation input to an int32_t
# phase and shifts a negative velocity term left the same way. Apple's clang
# reported none of these with -fwrapv (2026-10-05); the entries keep a
# toolchain that does report them from stopping on known quirks.
signed-integer-overflow:third_party/msfa/*
shift-base:third_party/msfa/*
signed-integer-overflow:third_party/felucca-fm6/*
shift-base:third_party/felucca-fm6/*
